<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Page-1" id="lRaA55iZEk8nktToTO-t">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1828" dy="851" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Hello Interview Delivery Framework&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Requirement Gathering (functional and non-functional)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Entity extraction&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. API or System Interface&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Data flow (Esp. if data engineering heavy question)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. HLD that satisfies functional requirements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6. Deep dives into non functional requirements&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="201" width="469" x="62" y="63" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Requirement Gathering" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="254" x="-168" y="347" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Functional" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="254" x="-203" y="391" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="1. Users are able to view list of problems available on Leetcode like platform (in a paginated fashion)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="604" x="-136" y="442" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="2. Users are able to view details of a specific problem (eg: description, sample input and output test cases etc)&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="772" x="-193" y="493" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-8" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="3. Users are able to code a solution in their preferred language (C++/Java/ Python) and get feedback on their solution (AC/TLE/MLE/WA etc)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="772" x="-113" y="544" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-9" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="4. Support for contests is there, in which a set of problems is given to candidates. And the candidates are ranked according to the solution time of the problems. Users are able to see live leaderboard" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="772" x="-103" y="605" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Non functional" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="254" x="-190" y="671" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-11" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="1. CAP theorem: AP System, Availabilty &amp;gt;&amp;gt; Consistency eg: if a new problem/submission is created, it is okay if it&#39;s eventually consistent" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="746" x="-108" y="712" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-12" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="2. Security and isolation: Different user submissions should be isolated from each other, also platform should have appropriate guardrails from OOM, timeouts etc" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="746" x="-108" y="763" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-13" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="3. Low latency leaderboard view, also dashboard should be fresh or near realtime" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="746" x="-263" y="834" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9MYm1bHpN9P42XVpgqMA-14" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;4. Scalable to support competitions with 100K users&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="447" x="-108" y="896" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
